      "anchorLocalId": "jiuwudaishi:034:p003",
      "ownerFinding": "Quotable descriptive witness, not a placeholder. 「王衍父子」 explicitly names Wang Yan together with his son: the 子 of 父子 is a direct source referent of p003, and s0007 has only one 子. The hold is a representation gap: p003 carries only an English surface (\"his son\") and the descriptive label 王衍之子, which is not verbatim, so the native rule had no Chinese span to match. Adding the Chinese kinship surface 子 at s0007 (occurrence 0) makes 「王衍父子」 admissible without inventing a name. Whether 父子 covers one son or several is a source-supported unknown; it does not contradict the record, and English \"father and son\" / \"his son\" is an acceptable reading, so no English repair.",
      "ownerDisposition": "supply-native-witness-surface",
      "proposedWitness": {
        "localId": "jiuwudaishi:034:p003",
        "book": "jiuwudaishi",
        "chapter": "034",
        "unitId": "s0007",
        "quote": "王衍父子"
      },
      "independentVerdict": "hold",
      "primaryWitnessUnits": [
        {
          "unitId": "s0007",
          "path": "data/jiuwudaishi/034.json",
          "zh": "西川王衍父子及偽署將相官吏，除已行刑憲外，一切釋放。",
          "enLiteral": "Wang Yan of Shu, father and son, and the falsely appointed generals, ministers, and officials, except those already punished under criminal law, were all released.",
          "enIdiomatic": "Wang Yan of Shu, his son, and Shu's puppet ministers and officials were freed except those already executed."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "caseId": "sha256:925c8c384017fb7fa86cea854320d114a3ee11b9629518cb50e0203059b9e964",
      "localId": "jiuwudaishi:034:p010",
      "canonicalPersonId": "per_TT90SGB056CNMRPB377R",
      "transportLocalPeople": [
        "jiuwudaishi:034:p010"
      ],
      "protectedLocalPeople": [
        "jiuwudaishi:034:p010"
      ],
      "anchorLocalId": "jiuwudaishi:034:p010",
      "ownerFinding": "Unnamed inferred placeholder. s0019 「存乂，郭崇韜之子婿也」 states only that Cunyi was Guo Chongtao's son-in-law; 子婿 is a lexicalized kinship term and its 子 is not a referent for a separate daughter actor (same class as 兄 inside 兄子 in the jiutangshu/072 precedent). No unit of the chapter quotes the daughter. The explicit son-in-law link p009→p006 stands on its own. Remove p010; keep claim 111 without intermediaryPersonIds. The idiomatic \"Cunyi had married Guo Chongtao's daughter\" is a faithful gloss of 子婿 and needs no repair.",
      "ownerDisposition": "accept-hold-propose-remove-inferred-person",
      "independentVerdict": "hold",
      "primaryWitnessUnits": [
        {
          "unitId": "s0019",
          "path": "data/jiuwudaishi/034.json",
          "zh": "存乂，郭崇韜之子婿也，故亦及於禍。",
          "enLiteral": "Cunyi was Guo Chongtao's son-in-law; hence he too met disaster.",
          "enIdiomatic": "Cunyi had married Guo Chongtao's daughter, so he fell with the Guo clan."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
